#    0: 'Validate provider JSON with bounded, audited envelope normalization.\n\n    Some OpenAI-compatible endpoints serialize the schema-constrained object a\n    second time or wrap the single object in a one-item array.  Accept exactly\n    those two wire envelopes, then validate the complete inner object against\n    the original Pydantic schema.  This does not repair fields or invent data.\n\n    ``QAResult.summary`` is explanatory text and is not used for routing or\n    authorization.  Some providers return an otherwise valid QA object with a\n    summary longer than the UI/storage bound.  Clamp only that field, then run\n    the complete schema again so status, issues, comparisons and unknown fields\n    remain strictly validated.\n    '
